  "details": "VRChat Version: 2021.2.3p1 Build 1102\nDescription of the bug: In holoport mode, avatars take several seconds to reach full speed\nSteps to reproduce:\n1. Create a world, and on the VRCWorld prefab, turn the run speed up to something noticeably enormous (like 256)\n2. Load in with holoport disabled; you'll be whizzing around at high speeds like expected.\n3. Load in again with holoport enabled, and watch how slowly your avatar moves towards the blue target.\n4. Try leading your avatar back and forth without 'ending' the holoport; gradually, they will actually increase speed until they're staying directly on top of the target because of how fast they're traveling. However, if you end that holoport and begin a new one, they'll be moving slowly again until a few seconds have passed, like last time.",
